      "naive_mean_stack_mad_over_ideal": 1.6273811788270516,
      "reading": "stack_analysis.json divides a temporal scatter (each raw frame about the per-pixel median across frames, 0.045919) by a spatial term (mean per-frame MAD / sqrt(N), 0.003584). That temporal scatter is essentially the MAD of the twelve per-frame background levels (0.047187, ratio 0.97), and those levels span 0.2564 MJy/sr, a factor of about 3.0. It measures the spread of the per-frame zeropoints, not detector noise. With the offsets removed the temporal scatter is 0.009057, that is 0.73x the per-frame spatial MAD, so the frames are not strongly time-variable once the constant per-frame levels are gone. The spatial excess of the naive stack is 1.63x over the independence prediction, and the shift-and-stack measures 1.31x, so the 12.8x is an estimator artifact and must not be quoted as the stack noise excess"
